G. Tournament analysis
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Relation: x -> y iff x retains more proof-critical side information.
vertices=8 edges=28 c3=0 hp=1
  score 7: exact LRC M/Farey/C27 labels
  score 6: PH extension-rank bad-child profile
  score 5: J37 local-global orbit split
  score 4: Beurling-Selberg labelled minorant
  score 3: Euler pentagonal sigma recurrence
  score 2: real-factor recombination subset ledger
  score 1: pentagonal-vs-tetrahedral degree split
  score 0: raw local face/count signature

Verdict:
  The common carrier is not a number.  It is labelled recombination under
  an extension/twist constraint: PH needs child-rank, J37 needs vertex-orbit
  data, Beurling-Selberg needs one-sided defect labels, Euler sigma needs
  pentagonal signs, and LRC14 needs C27/Farey labels before product analogies.
